# UnstableOS inittab format:
# id:runlevel:action:command

# id is used for logging of launched/dead/finished tasks
# runlevel is ignored for now
# action can be the following:
# 	once: runs once and reports exit status if it failed
# 	respawn: respawns the process if it dies
# 	wait: inittab parsing is put on hold until this process finishes
#   askfirst: like respawn, but asks for cr/lf on the terminal given by id
#   boot: same as once, but ignored on reloads
#   bootwait: same as wait, but ignore on reloads
#

# note: the command field does quoting the same way a shell might
# 	it is the only field that gets quoted

# if you really NEED to type #, do \#

getty0::respawn:getty 0 /dev/tty0
gettyS0::respawn:getty -L -w 115200 /dev/ttyS0
